{
  "name": "blast-visual-full",
  "description": "Comprehensive visual pipeline test covering all 7 blast system areas: drill plan, charge/sequence, software preview tiers, detonation execution, post-blast report, and voxel fragmentation with multi-angle screenshots at every stage",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42",
      "timeout": 15,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 50000,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "drill_plan grid rows:3 cols:4 spacing:5 depth:6 start:20,20",
      "description": "Two increment clicks on the spacing stepper (data-field=\"spacing\") raise it 3->5m (DEFAULT_SPACING_M, Drill.ts) before dragging, so the (20,20)-(35,30) rectangle computes the declared 4x3 instead of the default-spacing 6x4 (issue #479 follow-up, Finding #4). depth corrected from 8 to 6 (Ground rule #15/Finding #42's class, the whole-suite audit before Phase 3): this step never clicks the grid tool's depth stepper (data-field=\"depth\"), so the real drag always produces the panel's own 6m default regardless of what's declared. This file's own expect blocks only assert hole/charge/sequence counts around the affected blast (depth-insensitive), so this is a metadata-only correction -- verified both modes still pass unchanged.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"blast\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"1\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"grid-tool\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-param-strip [data-field=\"spacing\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-param-strip [data-field=\"spacing\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "dragTiles",
          "x1": 20,
          "z1": 20,
          "x2": 35,
          "z2": 30
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "holeCount": 12
        },
        "note": "3 rows x 4 cols = 12"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "drill_plan show",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "drill_plan show"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "charge hole:* explosive:boomite amount:5 stemming:2",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"2\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"charge-all\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "chargedCount": 12
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "charge hole:H1 explosive:boomite amount:8 stemming:3",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "assert",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-value",
          "property": "textContent",
          "expectedValue": "8 kg"
        },
        {
          "type": "assert",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-value",
          "property": "textContent",
          "expectedValue": "3.0 m"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-hole=\"H1\"] [data-action=\"charge-hole\"]"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Per-hole charging is a real control now (gap G3, ChargeHoleList.ts): the Charge step renders a \"Per Hole\" section, one row per hole keyed by data-hole, each with its own commit button at [data-hole=\"<id>\"] [data-action=\"charge-hole\"]. That button dispatches `charge hole:<id> explosive:<selected> amount:<amount>kg stemming:<stemming>m` from the panel's current product card / amount / stemming values (ChargeStep.chargeHole, Charge.ts) — the same three values Charge All reads, so the steppers have to be driven to the declared numbers first. The Charge All step above already pinned the panel to [data-step=\"2\"] (a manual tab click disarms autoAdvance), so the Per Hole rows stay visible. 3 amount increments (5 -> 8kg) and 5 stemming increments (2.0 -> 3.0m) reach this hole's declared values. Amount steps by 1kg (data-field=\"amount\", clamped to the selected product's [minChargeKg, maxChargeKg]); stemming steps by 0.2m with a 0.5m floor (data-field=\"stemming\", Charge.ts adjustStemming). Both are plain instance fields on ChargeStep with no reset path, so they carry over from the previous charge step in the same page session — asserted before each commit rather than assumed.",
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "chargedCount": 12
        },
        "note": "count is unchanged — every hole was already charged by Charge All; this step overrides H1 alone"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "charge hole:H2 explosive:boomite amount:3 stemming:1",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "assert",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-value",
          "property": "textContent",
          "expectedValue": "3 kg"
        },
        {
          "type": "assert",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-value",
          "property": "textContent",
          "expectedValue": "1.0 m"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-hole=\"H2\"] [data-action=\"charge-hole\"]"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The opposite override on the neighbouring hole: 5 amount decrements (8 -> 3kg) and 10 stemming decrements (3.0 -> 1.0m) off what the H1 row left behind, then H2's own commit button.",
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "chargedCount": 12
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence auto delay_step:25",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"3\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"auto-sequence\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "sequencedCount": 12
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence set hole:H1 delay:0",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-hole=\"H1\"] [data-action=\"delay-dec\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-hole=\"H1\"] [data-action=\"delay-dec\"]"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Per-hole delay is a relative +/- stepper ([data-hole=\"<id>\"] [data-action=\"delay-inc\"/\"delay-dec\"], Sequence.ts), stepping by the panel's current delay-step value and clamping at 0. Reaching an exact target is therefore arithmetic on the delay Auto Sequence actually assigned, read out of a real command-mode trace (screenshots/scenario-<name>-command/step-NN-sequence.json's sequenceDelays) rather than computed by re-deriving autoVPattern. Auto Sequence left H1 at 50ms with a 25ms step (traced: step-08-sequence.json), so 2 decrements land exactly on the declared 0 (50 -> 25 -> 0); a third would be a no-op, since adjustHoleDelay floors the result at 0.",
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "sequencedCount": 12
        },
        "note": "H1 50ms -> 25 -> 0; no hole gains or loses a delay, only H1's value changes"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence set hole:H6 delay:100",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-hole=\"H6\"] [data-action=\"delay-inc\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-hole=\"H6\"] [data-action=\"delay-dec\"]"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Auto Sequence already put H6 on exactly this step's declared 100ms (traced: step-08-sequence.json), so the arithmetic here is a net zero — one increment and one decrement (100 -> 125 -> 100) is the honest click expression of it, and it still exercises both stepper directions on a row other than H1. Command mode's version of this step was likewise a no-op: the step-08 and step-09 dumps are byte-identical.",
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "sequencedCount": 12
        },
        "note": "H6 ends on 100ms, the same value it started this step with"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence show",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "sequence show"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "blast_preview",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"4\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"run-analysis\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player"
    },
